      "content": "i see. so you're saying that the way to handle those \"not natural\" or \"confusing\" perspectives is basically to just brush them off and focus on acceptance? i guess i'm just wondering if there's any valid reason to wait or if there's actually any merit to the idea that kids might be better off without this kind of info. is it always the \"correct\" approach to dive into it?",
